<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://qconsulting.ca/fo3/ModConfig5.0.xsd">
	<moduleName>Fitting Room</moduleName>
	<moduleImage path="Images\fittingroom.png"/>

	<!-- One DLL loads on both SE 1.5.97 and AE 1.6.1130+, so there is no SE/AE
	     file choice. The only choice is the STARTING SETUP, and since
	     2026-08-11 it is settings and NOTHING ELSE: every option installs
	     exactly the same files and they differ only in which FittingRoom.ini is
	     written. Game files ONLY in the install directives: the docs (LICENSE +
	     README.txt) ship at the archive root, NOT installed to Data - flat docs
	     at the Data root collide across mods and show as overwrite conflicts in
	     MO2.

	     ⚠⚠ THE ESP AND THE LORE UNLOCK RULES USED TO RIDE THE CHOICE AND NOW DO
	     NOT, because a choice made at install time was deciding what the mod
	     could do for the rest of the save. Picking Freeform and later turning
	     Lore friendly on in the settings panel left a player with no Seamstone
	     to carry or pay with, and - the larger half - without
	     Unlocks\lore.json, so 80 colours fell back to their rarity tier and the
	     locked swatches said "Level 35" where they should name a quest. Neither
	     is a thing an installer page should be able to take away from a
	     playstyle switch (user 2026-08-11).

	     ⚠ THE COST OF SHIPPING THE ESP TO EVERYONE IS A LIGHT SLOT, NOT A REAL
	     ONE. FittingRoomLore.esp is ESL-flagged (header flag 0x200), 1695
	     bytes, and masters Skyrim.esm alone, so it lands in the FE space and
	     none of the 254 regular slots. It is also inert until the settings ask
	     for it: no requirement, no cost, an item sold by one merchant.

	     ⚠ AND lore.json IS SAFE IN CORE FOR A SEPARATE REASON. Unlock rules only
	     ever LOCK - a colour with no rule is FREE - so shipping more of them
	     cannot hand anything out, and with bDyeUnlocks off they gate nothing at
	     all. Freeform is unchanged by their presence and a later switch finds
	     the economy the design actually wrote.

	     ⚠⚠ THE PAGES QUESTION IS GONE AND EVERY PAGE SHIPS ON (user 2026-08-28).
	     It asked which of the eight sidebar tiles to start with and offered
	     three bundles: all of them, the wardrobe four, the character four. Two
	     of the three hid working pages from a player who had not yet seen one,
	     to save them a sidebar they could empty in the editor's own Pages tab in
	     a second. The installer was asking a question the answer to which is
	     always "show me, I will hide what I do not want", so it stopped asking
	     and the template's eight b*=1 keys are now the only answer. The axis
	     also cost twelve pre-baked INIs where there are now four. -->
	<requiredInstallFiles>
		<folder source="core\SKSE" destination="SKSE" priority="0"/>
		<folder source="core\Scripts" destination="Scripts" priority="0"/>
		<folder source="core\Interface" destination="Interface" priority="0"/>
		<folder source="core\textures" destination="textures" priority="0"/>
		<file source="core\FittingRoomLore.esp" destination="FittingRoomLore.esp" priority="0"/>
	</requiredInstallFiles>

	<installSteps order="Explicit">
		<installStep name="How should the Fitting Room open?">
			<optionalFileGroups order="Explicit">
				<group name="Starting setup (just settings, change any of it any time)" type="SelectExactlyOne">
					<plugins order="Explicit">
						<plugin name="Freeform">
							<description>Just the wardrobe. Your hotkey opens the Fitting Room in your inventory, changing an outfit is free, and you can dress out of nothing rather than needing real gear underneath.

FittingRoomLore.esp installs either way and sits idle until you ask for it. It is a light plugin, so it costs none of your 254 load order slots, and it adds one item to one merchant.</description>
							<image path="Images\free-form.png"/>
							<files/>
							<conditionFlags>
								<flag name="setup">freeform</flag>
							</conditionFlags>
							<typeDescriptor>
								<type name="Recommended"/>
							</typeDescriptor>
						</plugin>
						<plugin name="Lore friendly">
							<description>Dressing up costs you something. Carry the Seamstone to open the Fitting Room, and spend its enchantment charge for each slot you change when you apply an outfit. Previewing is always free.

The Seamstone is a carryable Alteration focus. Farengar Secret-Fire in Dragonsreach sells one.

It runs on charge like an enchanted weapon: soul gems refill it, T Charge works on it, and there is a Refill button in the editor. Its item card carries a meter, and the editor says what an Apply will cost before you commit. It starts empty, so feed it a soul gem before your first restyle.

Gold works too if you would rather pay in coin. One setting, three answers: nothing, gold, or the stone.

The next page asks about dyes separately. What styling costs and whether dyes are earned are two different questions.</description>
							<image path="Images\lore-friendly.png"/>
							<files/>
							<conditionFlags>
								<flag name="setup">lore</flag>
							</conditionFlags>
							<typeDescriptor>
								<type name="Optional"/>
							</typeDescriptor>
						</plugin>
					</plugins>
				</group>
			</optionalFileGroups>
		</installStep>

		<installStep name="Your character's face">
			<!-- ⚠⚠ ADDED 2026-08-29 WITH THE SAFE ANSWER AS THE DEFAULT, after
			     two players lost a face to the RaceMenu features on 1.1.2 in
			     one night: eyes replaced with ones they had not chosen, and a
			     second face drawn over the first. Both rolled back. THE LOOKS
			     PAGE IS THE DEFAULT SINCE 1.1.7 (user 2026-09-02): the face arc
			     fixed what caused both, the template ships the three keys on,
			     and the safe answer is now the one that substitutes.

			     ⚠ THIS SETS A STARTING POSITION, NOT A CAPABILITY. Every
			     option here writes ini keys the settings panel owns and can
			     change back in a click; nothing is removed from the build. An
			     install choice that gated a runtime setting is a mistake this
			     repo has already made once. -->
			<optionalFileGroups order="Explicit">
				<group name="How much may Fitting Room touch your face? (settings, change any of it any time)" type="SelectExactlyOne">
					<plugins order="Explicit">
						<plugin name="Looks page">
							<description>Turns on the Looks page and the face features behind it: save a whole character as one look, let a look load its RaceMenu preset and switch your race and sex, and have Fitting Room put your look back after something else overwrites it.

On by default since 1.1.7. If your eyes change on their own or a second face appears, the settings panel turns these off in a click.</description>
							<image path="Images\face-page.png"/>
							<files/>
							<conditionFlags>
								<flag name="face">full</flag>
							</conditionFlags>
							<typeDescriptor>
								<type name="Recommended"/>
							</typeDescriptor>
						</plugin>
						<plugin name="Leave my face alone">
							<description>Fitting Room never swaps a head part or loads a look's RaceMenu preset, and the Looks page is hidden, so nothing offers to rebuild a character you already built. Your colours are still put back after the game repaints your head.

Outfits, dyes, overlays and shapes all work exactly the same. Pick this if you have a face you like and want it left alone.</description>
							<image path="Images\face-page.png"/>
							<files/>
							<conditionFlags>
								<flag name="face">safe</flag>
							</conditionFlags>
							<typeDescriptor>
								<type name="Optional"/>
							</typeDescriptor>
						</plugin>
					</plugins>
				</group>
			</optionalFileGroups>
		</installStep>

		<installStep name="The dye colours">
			<!-- ⚠ ALL DYES UNLOCKED IS FIRST AND RECOMMENDED (user 2026-08-28). It
			     used to sit second behind Earn dyes. Most people arrive to dress a
			     character rather than to work through an economy, and the padlocks
			     are the surprising answer of the two, so the padlocks are the one
			     you now have to ask for. Both are still one tick in the settings
			     panel and neither takes anything back. -->
			<optionalFileGroups order="Explicit">
				<group name="Should dyes be earned? (a setting, change it any time)" type="SelectExactlyOne">
					<plugins order="Explicit">
						<plugin name="All dyes unlocked">
							<description>Every dye you have installed is yours from the start. No padlocks.

Pick this if you came to dress your character rather than to play an economy. Nothing you have earned is ever taken back, so turning the locks on later starts you from what you have.</description>
							<image path="Images\all-dyes.png"/>
							<files/>
							<conditionFlags>
								<flag name="colours">free</flag>
							</conditionFlags>
							<typeDescriptor>
								<type name="Recommended"/>
							</typeDescriptor>
						</plugin>
						<plugin name="Earn dyes">
							<description>The palette is something to work through. A dye opens up for what your character has done: quests finished, ruins cleared, skills raised. A locked swatch says what it takes, and a card appears at the top right when one arrives.

There are 458 of them, so there is a lot in there to find.</description>
							<image path="Images\earn-dyes.png"/>
							<files/>
							<conditionFlags>
								<flag name="colours">earn</flag>
							</conditionFlags>
							<typeDescriptor>
								<type name="Optional"/>
							</typeDescriptor>
						</plugin>
					</plugins>
				</group>
			</optionalFileGroups>
		</installStep>

		<installStep name="Before you play">
			<!-- ⚠ ONE PICTURE FOR BOTH OPTIONS ON THIS STEP, ON PURPOSE. Neither is
			     a choice: they are two paragraphs of reading on a page that sets no
			     flag and installs no file. Shooting the pair separately would give a
			     reader two frames to tell apart for no decision they are making.
			     This is NOT the case the shot list warns about, where three real
			     options shared the banner and a player choosing between them saw the
			     same image three times. -->
			<optionalFileGroups order="Explicit">
				<group name="Worth knowing" type="SelectAny">
					<plugins order="Explicit">
						<plugin name="An interface mod I recommend">
							<description>The vanilla layout puts the item card and the floating preview on the right of the screen, which is exactly where your character stands. Fitting Room hides the preview while its editor is open and leaves it alone otherwise.

A Vel'dun-style interface layout moves both well clear of them. Not required, not a dependency.</description>
							<image path="Images\worth-knowing.png"/>
							<files/>
							<typeDescriptor>
								<type name="Optional"/>
							</typeDescriptor>
						</plugin>
						<plugin name="Goes well with">
							<description>Menu Studio pauses the world and stages your character, which is what makes browsing outfits worth looking at.

Apparel Preview shows a piece on your character as you highlight it, before you commit.

Both optional. Fitting Room works on its own.

https://github.com/maartenharms/fitting-room

Thanks for installing. An endorsement is always appreciated if you enjoy it.</description>
							<image path="Images\worth-knowing.png"/>
							<files/>
							<typeDescriptor>
								<type name="Optional"/>
							</typeDescriptor>
						</plugin>
					</plugins>
				</group>
			</optionalFileGroups>
		</installStep>
	</installSteps>

	<!-- The two pages are INDEPENDENT AXES, so the starting INI is chosen by the
	     PAIR of answers rather than by either one alone. Four files, generated by
	     tools/make_fomod.sh from the one documented template with a guard on
	     every flip, because a hand-maintained fourth copy forks its comments the
	     first time anybody edits one of them.

	     Every pattern below matches exactly one combination and all four
	     combinations are covered. A missing pair would install NO ini, which is
	     survivable (the plugin writes its own on first run) and would silently
	     ignore the player's answers, which is not.

	     ⚠ THERE WERE TWELVE OF THESE UNTIL 2026-08-28, when the pages question
	     went. Three page bundles times these four is where the other eight came
	     from. -->
	<!-- ⚠⚠ EACH PATTERN INSTALLS ITS INI TWICE SINCE 1.1.7 (2026-09-02). The live
	     copy at SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini is what the plugin reads and writes,
	     and a leftover in Overwrite or in a mod above shadows it: measured on the
	     author's rig, where "Earn dyes" was answered here and never arrived. The
	     second copy, SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini, is a path the plugin
	     never writes, so nothing shadows it, and it carries a stamp naming the zip
	     and the answers; the plugin takes the eight answers from it once per
	     install. See InstallerSeed.h. -->
	<conditionalFileInstalls>
		<patterns>
			<pattern>
				<dependencies operator="And">
					<flagDependency flag="setup" value="lore"/>
					<flagDependency flag="colours" value="earn"/>
					<flagDependency flag="face" value="safe"/>
				</dependencies>
				<files>
					<file source="settings\lore-earn-safe\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini" priority="1"/>
					<file source="settings\lore-earn-safe\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini" priority="1"/>
				</files>
			</pattern>
			<pattern>
				<dependencies operator="And">
					<flagDependency flag="setup" value="lore"/>
					<flagDependency flag="colours" value="earn"/>
					<flagDependency flag="face" value="full"/>
				</dependencies>
				<files>
					<file source="settings\lore-earn-full\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini" priority="1"/>
					<file source="settings\lore-earn-full\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini" priority="1"/>
				</files>
			</pattern>
			<pattern>
				<dependencies operator="And">
					<flagDependency flag="setup" value="lore"/>
					<flagDependency flag="colours" value="free"/>
					<flagDependency flag="face" value="safe"/>
				</dependencies>
				<files>
					<file source="settings\lore-free-safe\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini" priority="1"/>
					<file source="settings\lore-free-safe\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini" priority="1"/>
				</files>
			</pattern>
			<pattern>
				<dependencies operator="And">
					<flagDependency flag="setup" value="lore"/>
					<flagDependency flag="colours" value="free"/>
					<flagDependency flag="face" value="full"/>
				</dependencies>
				<files>
					<file source="settings\lore-free-full\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini" priority="1"/>
					<file source="settings\lore-free-full\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini" priority="1"/>
				</files>
			</pattern>
			<pattern>
				<dependencies operator="And">
					<flagDependency flag="setup" value="freeform"/>
					<flagDependency flag="colours" value="earn"/>
					<flagDependency flag="face" value="safe"/>
				</dependencies>
				<files>
					<file source="settings\freeform-earn-safe\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini" priority="1"/>
					<file source="settings\freeform-earn-safe\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini" priority="1"/>
				</files>
			</pattern>
			<pattern>
				<dependencies operator="And">
					<flagDependency flag="setup" value="freeform"/>
					<flagDependency flag="colours" value="earn"/>
					<flagDependency flag="face" value="full"/>
				</dependencies>
				<files>
					<file source="settings\freeform-earn-full\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini" priority="1"/>
					<file source="settings\freeform-earn-full\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini" priority="1"/>
				</files>
			</pattern>
			<pattern>
				<dependencies operator="And">
					<flagDependency flag="setup" value="freeform"/>
					<flagDependency flag="colours" value="free"/>
					<flagDependency flag="face" value="safe"/>
				</dependencies>
				<files>
					<file source="settings\freeform-free-safe\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini" priority="1"/>
					<file source="settings\freeform-free-safe\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini" priority="1"/>
				</files>
			</pattern>
			<pattern>
				<dependencies operator="And">
					<flagDependency flag="setup" value="freeform"/>
					<flagDependency flag="colours" value="free"/>
					<flagDependency flag="face" value="full"/>
				</dependencies>
				<files>
					<file source="settings\freeform-free-full\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom.ini" priority="1"/>
					<file source="settings\freeform-free-full\FittingRoom.ini" destination="SKSE\Plugins\FittingRoom\installer.ini" priority="1"/>
				</files>
			</pattern>
		</patterns>
	</conditionalFileInstalls>
</config>
